1
00:01:52,612 --> 00:01:55,449
<i>Damn it.
Where did those chickens go?</i>

2
00:01:55,866 --> 00:01:58,660
<i>They couldn't have gotten far
in this downpour...</i>

3
00:02:00,454 --> 00:02:02,080
<i>I'm gonna find them,
no matter what.</i>

4
00:02:02,205 --> 00:02:04,499
<i>And get more footage
that goes viral, for sure!</i>

5
00:02:04,791 --> 00:02:08,669
I'll definitely become
a successful Viewtuber!

6
00:02:08,670 --> 00:02:11,089
No... I need to become one!

7
00:02:11,548 --> 00:02:12,591
<i>That's right...</i>

8
00:02:13,050 --> 00:02:16,637
<i>I haven't forgotten
the humiliation from then...</i>

9
00:02:17,179 --> 00:02:19,348
THREE MONTHS AGO

10
00:02:21,058 --> 00:02:23,018
Hey, Ibokura!

11
00:02:23,894 --> 00:02:25,854
The Chief was furious!

12
00:02:25,979 --> 00:02:28,189
Can't you write a proper report?

13
00:02:28,190 --> 00:02:30,233
There's no way anyone can
read this. Am I right?

14
00:02:31,485 --> 00:02:33,820
We had to rewrite it.

15
00:02:33,862 --> 00:02:35,739
Aren't you gonna thank us?

16
00:02:35,781 --> 00:02:39,618
You did that all
of your own volition.

17
00:02:39,868 --> 00:02:41,912
I don't owe you any thanks.

18
00:02:42,079 --> 00:02:42,913
What did you say?!

19
00:02:42,996 --> 00:02:44,581
Are you messing with us?

20
00:02:44,790 --> 00:02:46,291
I'm not messing around at all.

21
00:02:46,375 --> 00:02:48,585
Don't bother with him.

22
00:02:48,794 --> 00:02:52,756
He doesn't have the decency
to express any gratitude.

23
00:02:52,798 --> 00:02:56,259
All he has going for him is pride,
even though his work's sloppy.

24
00:02:56,385 --> 00:02:58,970
That's right.
You might catch his incompetence.

25
00:02:59,012 --> 00:03:01,055
I hope he quits soon.

26
00:03:01,056 --> 00:03:02,098
Loser.

27
00:03:02,099 --> 00:03:03,016
Salary leech...

28
00:03:03,100 --> 00:03:04,851
<i>Those pieces ofâ€“!</i>

29
00:03:04,976 --> 00:03:08,772
<i>I'm gonna show each and
every one of you!!</i>

30
00:03:11,525 --> 00:03:14,653
<i>I'll become a big,
successful viewtuber...</i>

31
00:03:14,778 --> 00:03:17,239
<i>And I'll show those scum!</i>

32
00:03:17,739 --> 00:03:20,617
That's why I need to
find those chickens!!

33
00:03:22,452 --> 00:03:25,288
Chickens!!

34
00:03:26,498 --> 00:03:29,292
EPISODE 6
BUILT LIKE A BRICK COOP

35
00:03:41,638 --> 00:03:43,348
This is not good!

36
00:03:58,447 --> 00:04:00,115
Are you okay, Grandpa?

37
00:04:00,657 --> 00:04:03,577
I'm finally feeling a bit better...

38
00:04:04,161 --> 00:04:07,122
I hope the Mister is okay.

39
00:04:07,497 --> 00:04:09,249
I'm worried.

40
00:04:11,793 --> 00:04:14,129
<i>I'm continuing my travels alone.</i>

41
00:04:15,088 --> 00:04:17,549
Did he really go off on his own?

42
00:04:17,883 --> 00:04:18,717
Everybody!

43
00:04:19,593 --> 00:04:21,135
Please stay calm and listen...

44
00:04:21,136 --> 00:04:21,969
What is it?

45
00:04:21,970 --> 00:04:23,054
- What happened?
- What?

46
00:04:23,263 --> 00:04:25,307
We've received word
from the state office.

47
00:04:25,640 --> 00:04:28,435
Due to getting 1000 milliliters-plus
of rainfall last night...

48
00:04:28,727 --> 00:04:31,520
There are fears that
Kurome Dam could collapse.

49
00:04:31,521 --> 00:04:32,439
What?!

50
00:04:34,733 --> 00:04:36,234
What does that mean?

51
00:04:36,485 --> 00:04:38,653
The water in the reservoir
is going to flood the town!

52
00:04:38,695 --> 00:04:39,613
What?!

53
00:04:40,197 --> 00:04:41,156
You're kidding!

54
00:04:41,239 --> 00:04:42,866
How could a dam that big
break so easily?!

55
00:04:42,908 --> 00:04:44,534
Actually, this reminds me...

56
00:04:44,576 --> 00:04:45,952
Back when the dam was first built,

57
00:04:45,994 --> 00:04:47,953
there was a rumor
that the dam was built cheaply

58
00:04:47,954 --> 00:04:48,830
and it caused a stir.

59
00:04:48,914 --> 00:04:50,999
You're kidding me!
Those scumbag builders!

60
00:04:51,041 --> 00:04:52,542
What should we do?!

61
00:04:52,709 --> 00:04:55,170
The state office told us to
continue taking shelter here.

62
00:04:55,295 --> 00:04:56,213
That's ridiculous!

63
00:04:56,338 --> 00:04:57,839
If all that water in
the dam floods,

64
00:04:57,923 --> 00:04:59,382
the whole town would
be submerged!

65
00:04:59,549 --> 00:05:01,343
We have to get out of town quickly!

66
00:05:01,551 --> 00:05:04,346
There's still a storm outside
and the river is flooding.

67
00:05:04,429 --> 00:05:06,473
We can't leave town right now.

68
00:05:06,556 --> 00:05:07,933
What are you doing?

69
00:05:08,099 --> 00:05:09,851
Trying to find a route to the dam.

70
00:05:09,976 --> 00:05:12,771
DAM
If we go there, there might be a way
to prevent it from breaking.

71
00:05:14,981 --> 00:05:15,941
Wait!

72
00:05:17,859 --> 00:05:19,361
I'm going too!

73
00:05:23,156 --> 00:05:25,867
Where did they go?

74
00:05:28,954 --> 00:05:30,038
It's that chicken!

75
00:05:30,539 --> 00:05:32,916
But I don't see the other one!

76
00:05:33,500 --> 00:05:36,086
No, I can't be picky right now.

77
00:05:36,586 --> 00:05:39,214
I gotta go after them.

78
00:05:41,258 --> 00:05:42,884
That dam's gonna break!

79
00:05:42,926 --> 00:05:44,553
Where should we go?!

80
00:05:45,887 --> 00:05:47,931
Crap! Where are they headed?!

81
00:05:49,349 --> 00:05:50,684
I see the dam!

82
00:05:53,520 --> 00:05:56,273
Is that a Demon?

83
00:06:00,151 --> 00:06:02,529
Why is that Demon...?

84
00:06:02,946 --> 00:06:04,990
Oh, I get it!

85
00:06:07,951 --> 00:06:10,579
Where did Elizabeth and Piyoko go?

86
00:06:10,787 --> 00:06:12,706
Everyone, look!

87
00:06:13,248 --> 00:06:15,792
It's a Demon!
A Demon's about to break the dam!

88
00:06:15,834 --> 00:06:17,419
What? Are you serious?!

89
00:06:17,460 --> 00:06:19,629
First, a flood, now a Demon?!

90
00:06:19,671 --> 00:06:20,881
Connect to the TV!

91
00:06:21,172 --> 00:06:25,176
Aren't Demons those
monster-like creatures?

92
00:06:25,677 --> 00:06:28,096
INPUT 2

93
00:06:26,845 --> 00:06:27,762
It's on!

94
00:06:28,179 --> 00:06:29,431
You're right, it's a Demon!

95
00:06:29,472 --> 00:06:30,640
Gimme a break!

96
00:06:30,724 --> 00:06:31,725
It's over!

97
00:06:31,850 --> 00:06:33,476
No, look closer.

98
00:06:33,643 --> 00:06:36,688
I think that Demon's trying to
prevent it from collapsing.

99
00:06:33,685 --> 00:06:40,650
INPUT 2

100
00:06:36,813 --> 00:06:37,646
What?!

101
00:06:37,647 --> 00:06:38,732
You're kidding...

102
00:06:38,773 --> 00:06:40,358
No, it's true!

103
00:06:40,400 --> 00:06:42,319
That Demon's holding it up!

104
00:06:42,360 --> 00:06:43,361
- What?!
- What?!

105
00:06:45,614 --> 00:06:46,448
Hang in there.

106
00:06:46,823 --> 00:06:48,282
- Hang in there, Demon!
- Please!

107
00:06:48,283 --> 00:06:49,783
- Hang in there, Demon!
- Hang in there!

108
00:06:49,784 --> 00:06:53,246
Hang in there!

109
00:06:53,747 --> 00:06:55,665
<i>Elizabeth and Piyoko?!</i>

110
00:06:55,915 --> 00:06:57,375
<i>What are they doing there?!</i>

111
00:07:02,213 --> 00:07:06,092
This is incredible!
The viewers keep pouring in!

112
00:07:09,638 --> 00:07:11,806
What are you doing?!

113
00:07:12,015 --> 00:07:13,224
It's dangerous here!

114
00:07:13,350 --> 00:07:14,809
Get out of here right now!

115
00:07:15,185 --> 00:07:16,936
You're a Demon, right?

116
00:07:17,228 --> 00:07:18,688
Why are you doing this?

117
00:07:19,981 --> 00:07:21,024
I...

118
00:07:21,149 --> 00:07:23,485
I want to save all the townsfolk!

119
00:07:24,569 --> 00:07:27,238
<i>Save... humans?</i>

120
00:07:33,203 --> 00:07:34,954
<i>Just keep on living.</i>

121
00:07:35,497 --> 00:07:38,208
<i>You'll stumble upon
your purpose soon enough.</i>

122
00:07:39,459 --> 00:07:42,003
<i>Keiji, I've found it.</i>

123
00:07:42,754 --> 00:07:46,383
<i>I've always wanted
to be useful.</i>

124
00:07:46,841 --> 00:07:49,552
<i>I finally realize that now.</i>

125
00:07:50,428 --> 00:07:53,890
Keiji, now I can hold
my head up high and say this...

126
00:07:54,557 --> 00:07:56,101
This...

127
00:07:56,142 --> 00:07:59,979
This is the reason I was born!

128
00:08:00,480 --> 00:08:03,358
I'll hold this dam up even
if it costs me my life!

129
00:08:03,400 --> 00:08:05,777
You all need to get out
of here quick!

130
00:08:06,319 --> 00:08:08,655
What a kind Demon.

131
00:08:08,988 --> 00:08:11,408
<i>I've only read about this online.</i>

132
00:08:11,658 --> 00:08:14,536
<i>So... demons like this
really do exist!</i>

133
00:08:15,245 --> 00:08:18,832
<i>I'm going to exterminate
the Demons.</i>

134
00:08:19,833 --> 00:08:23,044
<i>Does this mean... I was wrong?</i>

135
00:08:23,294 --> 00:08:24,421
Elizabeth!

136
00:08:24,587 --> 00:08:25,422
Look!

137
00:08:26,214 --> 00:08:28,508
A human?!
What's he doing here?

138
00:08:29,342 --> 00:08:30,343
Why?

139
00:08:31,803 --> 00:08:33,346
<i>What's with this guy?</i>

140
00:08:33,555 --> 00:08:36,099
<i>Why is he going this far
just to help humans?</i>

141
00:08:37,183 --> 00:08:39,060
<i>He's throwing his life on the line...</i>

142
00:08:39,227 --> 00:08:40,145
<i>Why?</i>

143
00:08:40,729 --> 00:08:43,022
<i>I could never...</i>

144
00:08:44,065 --> 00:08:44,899
<i>Mom...</i>

145
00:08:45,608 --> 00:08:47,444
<i>I want to become a lawyer.</i>

146
00:08:47,902 --> 00:08:50,405
<i>I want to help lots of people in need!</i>

147
00:08:51,072 --> 00:08:52,866
PASS THE EXAM

148
00:08:53,450 --> 00:08:58,121
REJECTION NOTICE

149
00:08:55,452 --> 00:08:57,704
I failed because of you, Mom...

150
00:08:58,705 --> 00:09:00,665
It's all your fault, Mom!

151
00:09:01,708 --> 00:09:06,212
<i>I realized I was blaming everyone
around me for my problems...</i>

152
00:09:06,796 --> 00:09:09,090
<i>But deep down... I knew.</i>

153
00:09:09,758 --> 00:09:12,302
I was the one who was
responsible for everything.

154
00:09:13,178 --> 00:09:15,513
I just didn't want to admit it.

155
00:09:36,951 --> 00:09:39,662
<i>Mom... I don't...</i>

156
00:09:40,330 --> 00:09:42,415
<i>I don't wanna die...</i>

157
00:09:42,874 --> 00:09:44,626
<i>I don't wanna die!</i>

158
00:09:58,515 --> 00:09:59,390
Keiji!

159
00:10:04,854 --> 00:10:05,980
Mister!

160
00:10:06,064 --> 00:10:06,898
Keiji!

161
00:10:11,653 --> 00:10:13,947
<i>That rooster... saved me?</i>

162
00:10:14,155 --> 00:10:15,115
Keiji!

163
00:10:15,198 --> 00:10:18,326
Did you come because you were
also worried about the dam?

164
00:10:20,161 --> 00:10:23,873
To think you were the one keeping
the dam from breaking, Morio!

165
00:10:24,207 --> 00:10:25,917
Look at me, Keiji!

166
00:10:26,084 --> 00:10:29,337
I'm protecting everyone in town!

167
00:10:29,420 --> 00:10:32,590
I had a reason to live after all!

168
00:10:32,715 --> 00:10:33,550
That's right.

169
00:10:33,758 --> 00:10:36,886
Without you, there would have
been many casualties.

170
00:10:37,637 --> 00:10:40,223
No doubt, you're a hero.

171
00:10:40,723 --> 00:10:43,893
M-Me? A hero?

172
00:10:44,894 --> 00:10:49,023
Those words are wasted on me...

173
00:10:49,232 --> 00:10:53,319
I just wanted to be useful.

174
00:10:54,904 --> 00:10:56,114
That's just like you.

175
00:11:05,915 --> 00:11:08,084
I'm... at my limit!

176
00:11:11,421 --> 00:11:13,173
Morio!

177
00:11:17,552 --> 00:11:18,553
Morio...

178
00:11:20,388 --> 00:11:21,222
This is bad!

179
00:11:21,264 --> 00:11:23,141
Over here, Elizabeth!

180
00:11:24,350 --> 00:11:26,477
Both of you, get somewhere safe!

181
00:11:26,686 --> 00:11:27,812
What about you, Keiji?!

182
00:11:27,896 --> 00:11:29,605
I'm going to stop the flood!!

183
00:11:29,606 --> 00:11:30,440
- What?!
- What?!

184
00:11:42,160 --> 00:11:44,954
It really collapsed.

185
00:11:46,623 --> 00:11:47,707
This can't be...

186
00:11:47,874 --> 00:11:49,250
No way...

187
00:11:49,459 --> 00:11:50,293
Honey...

188
00:11:50,460 --> 00:11:53,379
Dear Lord in heaven...

189
00:11:53,421 --> 00:11:54,254
I'm scared!

190
00:11:54,255 --> 00:11:55,088
No way...

191
00:11:55,089 --> 00:11:56,841
- It's okay...
- Are we going to die?

192
00:12:00,386 --> 00:12:01,429
<i>Are they running away?</i>

193
00:12:01,471 --> 00:12:02,512
<i>No.</i>

194
00:12:02,513 --> 00:12:04,641
<i>I can't imagine they would
turn a blind eye to this...</i>

195
00:12:05,016 --> 00:12:06,976
<i>They probably have
some sort of plan.</i>

196
00:12:07,060 --> 00:12:08,394
<i>I have to follow them!</i>

197
00:12:13,107 --> 00:12:15,693
<i>I did what I could.</i>

198
00:12:16,361 --> 00:12:19,864
<i>I hope I was useful to somebody.</i>

199
00:12:20,907 --> 00:12:21,741
<i>Keiji...</i>

200
00:12:22,242 --> 00:12:26,537
<i>Thanks to you,
I gained confidence in myself.</i>

201
00:12:27,455 --> 00:12:31,209
<i>I'm really glad I met you.</i>

202
00:12:33,002 --> 00:12:35,129
<i>Thanks a bunch, Keiji.</i>

203
00:12:35,672 --> 00:12:39,592
<i>I'm really glad I was born.</i>

204
00:12:41,552 --> 00:12:42,845
<i>I'm really glad...</i>

205
00:12:50,228 --> 00:12:51,062
<i>Morio...</i>

206
00:12:51,771 --> 00:12:54,274
<i>Those feelings that
you risked your life on...</i>

207
00:12:54,607 --> 00:12:56,734
<i>I won't let them go to waste!</i>

208
00:13:01,531 --> 00:13:08,538
Kokekokko!

209
00:13:10,331 --> 00:13:12,959
<i>What are you doing, Keiji?</i>

210
00:13:15,003 --> 00:13:16,296
I knew it!

211
00:13:17,130 --> 00:13:18,089
That rooster!

212
00:13:18,840 --> 00:13:20,008
I've seen him on Viewtube!

213
00:13:20,133 --> 00:13:23,052
Me too! It's the rooster
who defeated the Demon!

214
00:13:25,388 --> 00:13:26,681
You think...

215
00:13:26,806 --> 00:13:28,599
...he's trying to stop
the flood waters?

216
00:13:28,641 --> 00:13:29,684
That must be it!

217
00:13:29,767 --> 00:13:31,352
He must be trying to save us!

218
00:13:31,602 --> 00:13:33,021
Please stop the water, Rooster!

219
00:13:33,104 --> 00:13:34,731
Please, Rooster!

220
00:13:36,024 --> 00:13:39,569
<i>Is he a friend
of Elizabeth and Piyoko's?</i>

221
00:13:44,323 --> 00:13:45,742
- He made a wall!
- He made a wall!

222
00:13:52,373 --> 00:13:54,000
Please hold!!

223
00:14:02,508 --> 00:14:03,926
No way...

224
00:14:03,968 --> 00:14:04,969
It can't be...

225
00:14:05,178 --> 00:14:07,305
<i>A little wall like that won't cut it.</i>

226
00:14:08,056 --> 00:14:10,349
<i>I need something sturdier!</i>

227
00:14:10,600 --> 00:14:12,185
<i>Something sturdier!</i>

228
00:14:13,269 --> 00:14:14,103
That's it!

229
00:14:17,940 --> 00:14:19,692
He's so fast!

230
00:14:21,027 --> 00:14:22,570
What? Is he making another wall?

231
00:14:22,612 --> 00:14:24,363
It's not going to hold!

232
00:14:24,697 --> 00:14:26,616
But we're already so close to town!

233
00:14:26,866 --> 00:14:28,826
We need to stop it here, or else!

234
00:14:29,202 --> 00:14:30,953
Oh, I get it!

235
00:14:31,120 --> 00:14:32,330
That boulder!

236
00:14:32,413 --> 00:14:33,247
What?!

237
00:14:33,581 --> 00:14:37,043
He's going to drop that boulder
and block the water's path!

238
00:14:37,460 --> 00:14:40,671
A mass of rock that big
should withstand the water.

239
00:14:40,838 --> 00:14:44,300
Amazing... He's a genius!

240
00:14:47,637 --> 00:14:50,431
I see, he's going to bring it down.

241
00:14:52,767 --> 00:14:55,561
But isn't it too big?
Will he make it in time?!

242
00:15:01,067 --> 00:15:02,401
Hurry, Keiji!

243
00:15:02,443 --> 00:15:03,986
The water's here!

244
00:15:12,745 --> 00:15:13,579
Keiji!

245
00:15:13,663 --> 00:15:14,831
Mister!

246
00:15:18,709 --> 00:15:19,544
<i>Keiji...</i>

247
00:15:19,919 --> 00:15:23,005
Hang in there, Mister!

248
00:15:24,549 --> 00:15:26,175
Hang in there...

249
00:15:26,259 --> 00:15:27,343
Hang in there, Rooster!

250
00:15:27,426 --> 00:15:28,302
Hang in there!

251
00:15:28,344 --> 00:15:30,012
We're counting on you, Rooster!

252
00:15:30,805 --> 00:15:33,558
<i>Please, Mr. Rooster...</i>

253
00:15:33,850 --> 00:15:34,684
<i>Hang in there!</i>

254
00:15:38,312 --> 00:15:40,398
<i>This is just like the day we met.</i>

255
00:15:41,107 --> 00:15:44,277
<i>You didn't know us,
but you saved us.</i>

256
00:15:45,444 --> 00:15:47,071
<i>It seems you're the kind of man</i>

257
00:15:47,155 --> 00:15:51,450
<i>who can't help
but rescue those in need.</i>

258
00:15:53,286 --> 00:15:55,079
<i>I finally realize it now!</i>

259
00:15:55,788 --> 00:15:57,582
<i>That I...</i>

260
00:15:58,666 --> 00:15:59,959
<i>Love you!</i>

261
00:16:16,392 --> 00:16:17,268
What?!

262
00:16:19,687 --> 00:16:20,771
I'm not done yet!

263
00:16:21,689 --> 00:16:23,024
Is that the spot?!

264
00:16:30,031 --> 00:16:31,574
Keiji!

265
00:16:31,741 --> 00:16:33,659
Mister!

266
00:16:37,747 --> 00:16:39,040
You're kidding...

267
00:16:39,207 --> 00:16:40,208
No!

268
00:16:46,422 --> 00:16:49,759
Mister... the Mister is...!

269
00:16:49,926 --> 00:16:50,801
What's that?

270
00:16:55,556 --> 00:16:56,974
N-No way...

271
00:17:12,198 --> 00:17:17,161
Super Kokekkoko!

272
00:17:37,723 --> 00:17:39,308
He stopped it.

273
00:17:41,185 --> 00:17:43,771
How dare they make such
a crummy dam.

274
00:17:45,022 --> 00:17:46,983
It really makes my crown curl

275
00:17:52,655 --> 00:17:55,533
<i>Morio... We stopped it...</i>

276
00:17:55,783 --> 00:17:57,827
It's stopped!

277
00:17:59,036 --> 00:18:00,705
It's stopped!

278
00:18:00,788 --> 00:18:02,957
We're safe!

279
00:18:03,082 --> 00:18:04,125
Honey!

280
00:18:04,292 --> 00:18:05,126
Yeah.

281
00:18:05,376 --> 00:18:08,004
Thank you, God,
thank you, Buddha,

282
00:18:08,087 --> 00:18:10,965
Rooster! Rooster!

283
00:18:12,341 --> 00:18:15,970
It's a good thing
we let him get away.

284
00:18:16,012 --> 00:18:17,179
Yeah...

285
00:18:18,347 --> 00:18:22,101
<i>Elizabeth, Piyoko,
Mr. Rooster...</i>

286
00:18:22,810 --> 00:18:24,854
<i>Thank you for saving us.</i>

287
00:18:25,396 --> 00:18:28,316
<i>I promise to become a great doctor.</i>

288
00:18:29,233 --> 00:18:30,234
<i>So one day,</i>

289
00:18:30,401 --> 00:18:33,738
<i>I can help lots of people,
just like you did.</i>

290
00:18:34,655 --> 00:18:37,241
<i>Be well, my chicken friends.</i>

291
00:18:38,034 --> 00:18:40,119
Misuzu! Come over here!

292
00:18:40,161 --> 00:18:41,662
Oh, okay!

293
00:18:45,082 --> 00:18:47,168
Mister!

294
00:18:47,460 --> 00:18:49,295
Great job!

295
00:18:49,420 --> 00:18:51,922
I love you!

296
00:18:53,215 --> 00:18:54,091
What?!

297
00:18:54,967 --> 00:18:56,844
Uh, Piyoko...

298
00:18:56,969 --> 00:18:59,513
Don't you think
that's enough kissing?

299
00:18:59,722 --> 00:19:03,893
What's wrong with me wanting
to kiss my own husband?

300
00:19:04,935 --> 00:19:06,771
Did you say "your husband"?

301
00:19:06,896 --> 00:19:09,649
I think you might be the only one
who thinks that.

302
00:19:09,815 --> 00:19:11,942
By any chance, Elizabeth...

303
00:19:12,485 --> 00:19:15,029
...are you falling in love with him?

304
00:19:16,822 --> 00:19:18,574
That's silly!

305
00:19:18,949 --> 00:19:21,285
<i>Why is this child so perceptive?</i>

306
00:19:21,369 --> 00:19:23,788
Then why are you blushing?

307
00:19:23,829 --> 00:19:25,081
It's weird!

308
00:19:25,748 --> 00:19:27,166
You're imagining things!

309
00:19:27,291 --> 00:19:28,376
Liar!

310
00:19:28,542 --> 00:19:30,211
I'm not lying!

311
00:19:30,378 --> 00:19:32,004
You were!

312
00:19:32,129 --> 00:19:33,214
<i>No, I wasn't!</i>

313
00:19:33,339 --> 00:19:34,590
<i>Cut the racket.</i>

314
00:19:37,093 --> 00:19:37,927
Mom?

315
00:19:39,178 --> 00:19:40,638
It was a bad storm.

316
00:19:41,055 --> 00:19:41,889
Yeah.

317
00:19:42,223 --> 00:19:43,516
Oh, I'm fine.

318
00:19:44,141 --> 00:19:47,645
So... I've decided to continue traveling
for a while.

319
00:19:48,396 --> 00:19:49,480
Viewtube?

320
00:19:49,563 --> 00:19:51,482
I realized it wasn't my calling.

321
00:19:52,692 --> 00:19:53,526
Yeah.

322
00:19:53,943 --> 00:19:55,277
I'm totally sure.

323
00:19:56,028 --> 00:20:00,032
While traveling, I want to confront
my insecurities head-on...

324
00:20:00,783 --> 00:20:02,952
...to become a strong person.

325
00:20:04,245 --> 00:20:07,289
Yeah. I'll call you again soon.
Talk to you later.

326
00:20:10,459 --> 00:20:13,045
<i>Hey, Rooster... I'm gonna change.</i>

327
00:20:14,004 --> 00:20:16,590
<i>I'm gonna become someone who
can protect people just like you.</i>

328
00:20:17,633 --> 00:20:20,177
<i>Rooster... Demon...</i>

329
00:20:21,679 --> 00:20:23,472
<i>I can say it earnestly now...</i>

330
00:20:25,433 --> 00:20:27,852
<i>Thank you for helping me
realize everything!</i>

331
00:20:29,437 --> 00:20:31,021
By the way, Keiji...

332
00:20:31,605 --> 00:20:34,567
I thought you only cared
about avenging Sarah.

333
00:20:34,984 --> 00:20:36,193
How did you end up here?

334
00:20:36,736 --> 00:20:39,155
ONE HOUR EARLIER

335
00:20:39,363 --> 00:20:41,991
<i>Something feels completely off.</i>

336
00:20:42,491 --> 00:20:43,324
Hurry!

337
00:20:43,325 --> 00:20:45,119
- The dam is going to collapse!
- Be careful!

338
00:20:46,871 --> 00:20:48,164
<i>The dam is collapsing?</i>

339
00:20:48,706 --> 00:20:50,666
<i>Does that mean this town
will get submerged?</i>

340
00:20:50,916 --> 00:20:51,751
<i>Keiji!</i>

341
00:20:51,834 --> 00:20:52,668
<i>Mister!</i>

342
00:20:53,711 --> 00:20:55,796
<i>I'll never find them in time.</i>

343
00:20:56,464 --> 00:20:57,423
<i>In that case...</i>

344
00:20:58,466 --> 00:21:00,384
<i>I'll have to stop the flooding!</i>

345
00:21:03,679 --> 00:21:05,806
I was just passing by, that's all.

346
00:21:07,099 --> 00:21:08,476
<i>You're such a bad liar.</i>

347
00:21:14,523 --> 00:21:15,399
Morio...

348
00:21:15,691 --> 00:21:18,527
He was a kind Demon.

349
00:21:18,903 --> 00:21:21,071
I guess Demons like him actually
existed...

350
00:21:23,324 --> 00:21:25,910
I said once before that I wanted
to eliminate all Demons,

351
00:21:26,118 --> 00:21:27,703
but I take that back.

352
00:21:38,589 --> 00:21:41,759
<i>The sake we shared was the best.</i>

353
00:21:43,344 --> 00:21:45,638
<i>Farewell, Morio.</i>

354
00:21:55,272 --> 00:21:56,106
What?

355
00:21:58,025 --> 00:21:58,984
I'm alive?

356
00:22:00,736 --> 00:22:04,156
I'm alive!

357
00:22:06,742 --> 00:22:09,662
Look at how resilient I am!

358
00:22:09,995 --> 00:22:12,331
I'm alive!

359
00:22:14,333 --> 00:22:17,920
Huh? Wait,
why's the floodwater stopped?!

360
00:22:21,006 --> 00:22:21,966
It was Keiji!

361
00:22:25,302 --> 00:22:27,179
Hey!

362
00:22:27,805 --> 00:22:29,347
Hey!

363
00:22:29,348 --> 00:22:30,723
Morio?!

364
00:22:30,724 --> 00:22:31,891
It's the kind Demon!

365
00:22:31,892 --> 00:22:33,853
Keiji!

366
00:22:34,061 --> 00:22:36,480
That son of a bitch is still alive!

367
00:22:36,856 --> 00:22:40,067
You stopped the flooding, right?

368
00:22:40,609 --> 00:22:42,653
Thank you!

369
00:22:43,237 --> 00:22:45,364
Come visit again!

370
00:22:45,906 --> 00:22:50,870
I'll treat you to
some fresh sea urchin!

371
00:22:53,455 --> 00:22:56,166
Let's drink some more sake again!

372
00:22:56,709 --> 00:23:00,004
Yup! Let's meet again!

373
00:23:09,179 --> 00:23:10,472
There they go.

374
00:23:22,860 --> 00:23:25,029
Who... Who are you?!

375
00:23:50,304 --> 00:23:51,513
Keiji's going
on a group date?

376
00:23:51,722 --> 00:23:53,057
I hope he'll be okay...

377
00:23:53,432 --> 00:23:55,726
What do you do
on a "group date"?

378
00:23:56,185 --> 00:23:57,561
Well, uh...

379
00:23:57,645 --> 00:23:59,687
Next time:
Crowing Over a Feather

380
00:23:59,688 --> 00:24:01,315
You just changed the subject!

381
00:24:01,482 --> 00:24:03,859
- Tell me what it is!
- I don't know!

382
00:24:04,860 --> 00:24:09,782
FAN ART CONTEST AWARDS

